# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# Nothing here is ever printed by the scripts, written into a generated file, or
# committed. If you would rather not have a secret on disk at all, set the same
# names as environment variables in your shell instead — the scripts read the
# environment first and only fall back to this file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Needed for FOUR tables that RLS closes to the anon key:
#   price_snapshot, push_subscriptions, push_alerts, telegram_alerts
#
# Without it those four are skipped — `backfill build` says so by name rather
# than finishing quietly and leaving you with a load that looks complete.
#
# WHERE: Supabase dashboard → your project → Project Settings (the gear, bottom
#        left) → API → "Project API keys" → the `service_role` key → Reveal.
#
# It bypasses RLS entirely. It belongs here and in Render's environment, and
# nowhere else — never in the app bundle, never in a browser.
#
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=


# ── SUPABASE_DB_URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Postgres connection string, for taking the pg_dump backup.
#
# WHERE: Supabase dashboard → your project → Connect (top of the page) →
#        "Connection string" → the **Session pooler** tab. Copy the URI.
#
# It arrives with a placeholder for the password:
#
#   postgresql://postgres.dlzqdmqkvlvwnjhqxqym:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-...
#                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
#
# Replace that, brackets included, with your database password. It is NOT the
# service key and not your Supabase account password — it is set under Project
# Settings → Database → "Database password", where you can also reset it if you
# no longer have it. A reset breaks nothing that is running: the app connects
# over the REST API with the keys above, not with this.
#
# Session pooler rather than direct connection because the direct host is
# IPv6-only on the free plan, and the failure looks like a hang rather than an
# error. If the password contains @ : / or ?, percent-encode it.
#
SUPABASE_DB_URL=


# ── DATA_HUB_URL and DATA_HUB_SERVICE_SECRET ─────────────────────────────────
#
# For `backfill push`, which sends rows too large for a single SQL statement
# through the Worker's write path instead of a file.
#
# The URL is the deployed Worker. The secret is the SERVICE_SECRET that was set
# with `wrangler secret put` — Cloudflare will not show it again, so if it is
# lost, set a new one; that is a rotation, not a recovery.
#
DATA_HUB_URL=https://euro-trade-data.vxbtc.workers.dev
DATA_HUB_SERVICE_SECRET=
